{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/proposal.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Proposal\n\n## Why\n\n`Flask.run` splits `SERVER_NAME` at its first colon, so a bracketed IPv6\nliteral is passed to the development server with an invalid host and port.\n\n## What Changes\n\n- Parse bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` values when selecting default development\n  server host and port.\n- Preserve existing hostname, explicit port, and port-zero behavior.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n\n- `development-server-defaults`: Default host and port selection for\n  `Flask.run` from application configuration.\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n\n- None.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Affects `src/flask/app.py` and the `Flask.run` configuration tests in\n  `tests/test_basic.py`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
