{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/proposal.md; sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/specs/development-server-defaults/spec.md; sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/design.md; sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/tasks.md; grep -RIn \\\"partition(\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\")\\\" src/flask\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/proposal.md; sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/specs/development-server-defaults/spec.md; sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/design.md; sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/fix-server-name-ipv6-run/tasks.md; grep -RIn \\\"partition(\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\")\\\" src/flask\"","aggregated_output":"# Proposal\n\n## Why\n\n`Flask.run` splits `SERVER_NAME` at its first colon, so a bracketed IPv6\nliteral is passed to the development server with an invalid host and port.\n\n## What Changes\n\n- Parse bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` values when selecting default development\n  server host and port.\n- Preserve existing hostname, explicit port, and port-zero behavior.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n\n- `development-server-defaults`: Default host and port selection for\n  `Flask.run` from application configuration.\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n\n- None.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Affects `src/flask/app.py` and the `Flask.run` configuration tests in\n  `tests/test_basic.py`.\n# Spec Delta\n\n## Purpose\n\nDefines how development server defaults are selected from application\nconfiguration when `Flask.run` is called without a host or port.\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Bracketed IPv6 server-name defaults\nWhen `SERVER_NAME` is a bracketed IPv6 literal followed by a port, `Flask.run`\nMUST use the unbracketed IPv6 address as its default host and that port as its\ndefault port.\n\n#### Scenario: Run with an IPv6 server name\n- **WHEN** `SERVER_NAME` is set to `[::1]:8080` and `Flask.run` receives no\n  explicit host or port\n- **THEN** the development server receives host `::1` and port `8080`\n# Design\n\n## Context\n\n`Flask.run` currently obtains host and port defaults by splitting\n`SERVER_NAME` at the first colon. See proposal.md for motivation and the\ndevelopment-server-defaults spec for the required behavior.\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n\n- Recognize bracketed IPv6 literals with ports when deriving run defaults.\n- Retain the existing behavior for ordinary host names and port `0`.\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n\n- Changing URL routing or general `SERVER_NAME` handling outside `Flask.run`.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Treat a value beginning with `[` as a bracketed host, splitting it at the\n  closing bracket and removing the brackets before passing the host to the\n  server. This follows the documented host:port representation and avoids\n  treating an IPv6 address's internal colons as a port separator.\n- Keep the current first-colon split for non-bracketed values, preserving\n  existing hostname behavior.\n\n## Risks / Trade-offs\n\n- [Malformed bracketed values] → Preserve the current fallback behavior unless\n  a valid closing bracket and port separator are present.\n# Tasks\n\n## 1. Development server defaults\n\n- [ ] 1.1 Parse bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` values into an unbracketed host and port while retaining existing host parsing; verify the focused public test suite passes.\n- [ ] 1.2 Add the IPv6 default-host-and-port case to the existing `Flask.run` configuration test parametrization; verify it asserts host `::1` and port `8080`.\n\n## 2. Verification\n\n- [ ] 2.1 Run `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_basic.py -q` and verify the public basic test suite passes.\nsrc/flask/app.py:724:            sn_host, _, sn_port = server_name.partition(\":\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
